      "knowledge_point_id": "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables",
      "problem": "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$",
      "worked_solution": "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
